    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0378" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/10–1351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thompson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-13T12:00:00+01:00">October 13,
                            1951—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1694. In an after-dinner conversation last night, the Prime Minister asked me to
                    forward the following suggestion:</p>
                <p>He believes that we miss a propaganda advantage by constantly being forced to
                    take a negative attitude to Soviet proposals. He, therefore, suggests that
                    instead of saying no to the Soviet suggestion that Bulgaria, Hungary and Rumania
                    be admitted to the UN, we should state that we would welcome and support their
                    applications for membership as soon as they can produce evidence that they are
                    free and democratic.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 1694; repeated info Moscow 30.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thompson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
